// D1 round 5 / H7 — THE CLOSED EDGE OF F4's RESIDUAL CLASS.
//
// F4's residual is a CLASS, not the three types its old text named: a COMPOUND
// whose borrow-carrying is INFERRED from a type-arg / element / field position
// (tuple, array, plain struct, Box<&T>, Option<&T>) returns a reference to a
// local and still compiles. That is a recorded decision — both attempts to
// close it traded the leak for a wave of refusals of correct stdlib code — and
// it is NOT pinned here, because an `.expected` asserting a clean compile of
// unsound code records the defect as intended.
//
// What IS pinned is the class's BOUNDARY, and this is one of its two edges:
// the same struct marked `#[borrow_carrying]` — borrow-carrying DECLARED
// rather than inferred — refuses. The residual is exactly the inferred side of
// that line, and a red here would mean the line itself has moved.
//
// The other edge is pass/bc_d1r5_h7_param_root_admits.
package bc_d1r5_h7_declared_bc_struct_held;
#[borrow_carrying]
struct Pair { a: &i64, n: i64 }
fn f() -> Pair {
    let z: i64 = 1i64;
    return Pair { a: &z, n: 0i64 };
}
fn main() -> i64 { return 0i64; }
